This library provides convenient access to the OpenAI REST API from TypeScript or JavaScript.

It is generated from our OpenAPI specification.

To learn how to use the OpenAI API, check out our API Reference and Documentation.

```
npm install openai
```

### Installation with Deno

Deno can import the package directly from npm:

```
import OpenAIfrom'npm:openai';
```

The full API of this library can be found in api.md file along with many code examples. [...] const client = new OpenAI({
  apiKey: process.env['OPENAI_API_KEY'], // This is the default and can be omitted
});

const response = await client.responses.create({
  model: 'gpt-5.5',
  input: [
    {
      role: 'user',
      content: [
        { type: 'input_text', text: 'What is in this image?' },
        {
          type: 'input_image',
          detail: 'auto',
          image_url:
            '
        },
      ],
    },
  ],
});

console.log(response.output_text);
``` [...] 1. Changes that only affect static types, without breaking runtime behavior.
2. Changes to library internals which are technically public but not intended or documented for external use. (Please open a GitHub issue to let us know if you are relying on such internals.)
3. Changes that we do not expect to impact the vast majority of users in practice.

We take backwards-compatibility seriously and work hard to ensure you can rely on a smooth upgrade experience.
